KEY CONCEPT
📚 Lesson: Understanding DNS, Web Server, and Email System (Lab Overview)
🧠 What are we building?
In this lab, we are creating a mini version of the internet inside our network. 
This helps us understand how websites, emails, and domain names work together in real life.

🔑 The 3 Main Components
🌐 1. DNS (Domain Name System) – “The Phonebook”
DNS translates human-friendly names into IP addresses.
•	Example:
o	www.mylab.local → 192.168.1.10
o	mail.mylab.local → 192.168.1.20
👉 Without DNS, users would need to remember IP addresses instead of names.

🌍 2. Web Server (IIS) – “The Website Host”
This is where websites are stored and displayed.
•	When a user visits a domain (like www.mylab.local), the web server:
o	Receives the request
o	Shows the webpage
👉 In this lab, we created a sample or fake website for testing and learning.
📬 3. Mail Server (hMailServer) – “The Post Office”
This system handles email sending and receiving.
•	It:
o	Creates email accounts (e.g., user@mylab.local)
o	Sends emails (SMTP)
o	Receives emails (IMAP/POP3)
👉 It works in the background and stores all messages.

🖥️ 4. Mail Client (Thunderbird) – “The Email App”
This is what users interact with.
•	Used to:
o	Send emails
o	Read emails
o	View inbox
👉 It connects to the mail server to display messages.

