Step 2.1: Removing Auto-ban Session in hMailServer
Why we disable Auto-ban in this setup
The Auto-ban feature is a security mechanism. It automatically blocks (bans) an IP address if there are too many failed login attempts within a short time. This helps protect against brute-force attacks.
However, in a learning environment:
o	We make frequent mistakes 
While testing email clients, SMTP/IMAP settings, or passwords, it’s normal to enter incorrect credentials multiple times.
o	Shared networks cause unintended bans 
We may be working from the same network (same public IP). If one student triggers the limit, everyone on that network can get blocked.
o	It interrupts learning 
Once banned, connections will fail without clear feedback, making troubleshooting confusing and frustrating.
•	To fix this, go to Settings, under settings click Advanced, under Advanced click Auto-ban
[16.1]<Image placeholder>
•	Uncheck the enabled button for Auto-ban then click Save
[17.1]<Image placeholder>
•	The enabled button should now be disabled
